{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And [the Israelites] saw.</b> Now this is the sense of <b>And Moses put the veil back:</b> and so he did always, and thus was his practice with Israel until the day that the glory of HaShem was gathered to him. And his burial was not known, as HaShem had compassion upon him — blessed be He who chose him, and placed His holy spirit within him."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:29.382311383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}